  "claim": "Bengaluru Vijaya \"B.V.\" Radha starting her career in a 1964 Kannada film. The film was based on the life of the creator of the music form Geetam, who was born on Octover13, 1484.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Navakoti Narayana. Sentence: Navakoti Narayana (Kannada: ನವಕೋಟಿ ನಾರಾಯಣ ) is a 1964 Indian Kannada film directed by S. K. Ananthachari starring Rajkumar and Sowcar Janaki in lead roles.\nPage: Navakoti Narayana. Sentence: The film is based on the life of Purandara Dasa, a prominent composer of Carnatic music who lived from 1484-1564.\nPage: Purandara Dasa. Sentence: Purandara Dāsa (Kannada: ಪುರಂದರ ದಾಸ ) (1484–1564) was a Haridasa (a devotee - servant of Lord Hari (Vishnu)), great devotee of Lord Krishna (an incarnation of Lord Vishnu) and a saint.\nPage: B. V. Radha. Sentence: Starting her career in the 1964 Kannada film \"Navakoti Narayana\".\nPage: Geetam. Sentence: Geetam, (Sanskrit: गीतं; gītaṃ) the simplest music form in Carnatic music, was created by Purandara Dasa in order to introduce \"talas\" with \"sāhityaṃ\" (lyrics).",
