        "original_id": "e6b56c87-e4ce-5b9b-8300-6e3d79dae4dc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Navakoti Narayana\n- People: S. K. Ananthachari, Rajkumar, Sowcar Janaki, Purandara Dasa, B. V. Radha\n- Concepts: Carnatic music, Haridasa, Geetam\n\nFacts:\n- Purandara Dasa lived from 1484 to 1564.\n- Purandara Dasa was a Haridasa, a devotee of Lord Hari (Vishnu), a great devotee of Lord Krishna, and a saint.\n- Purandara Dasa was a prominent composer of Carnatic music.\n- Purandara Dasa created Geetam, the simplest music form in Carnatic music, to introduce talas with sahityam.\n- Navakoti Narayana is a 1964 Indian Kannada film directed by S. K. Ananthachari.\n- Navakoti Narayana stars Rajkumar and Sowcar Janaki in the lead roles.\n- Navakoti Narayana is based on the life of Purandara Dasa.\n- B. V. Radha started her career in the 1964 Kannada film Navakoti Narayana.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c3ffa9cb-c66d-5d2c-a929-d5df1b6dfe8f",
        "text": "Page: Navakoti Narayana. Sentence: Navakoti Narayana (Kannada: ನವಕೋಟಿ ನಾರಾಯಣ ) is a 1964 Indian Kannada film directed by S. K. Ananthachari starring Rajkumar and Sowcar Janaki in lead roles.\nPage: Navakoti Narayana. Sentence: The film is based on the life of Purandara Dasa, a prominent composer of Carnatic music who lived from 1484-1564.\nPage: Purandara Dasa. Sentence: Purandara Dāsa (Kannada: ಪುರಂದರ ದಾಸ ) (1484–1564) was a Haridasa (a devotee - servant of Lord Hari (Vishnu)), great devotee of Lord Krishna (an incarnation of Lord Vishnu) and a saint.\nPage: B. V. Radha. Sentence: Starting her career in the 1964 Kannada film \"Navakoti Narayana\".\nPage: Geetam. Sentence: Geetam, (Sanskrit: गीतं; gītaṃ) the simplest music form in Carnatic music, was created by Purandara Dasa in order to introduce \"talas\" with \"sāhityaṃ\" (lyrics).",
